+# First higher scalar images through rank five
+
+This is a new full mathematical candidate, pending independent exact review. Every earlier frozen module remains unchanged.
+
+The new source first_higher_images.tex proves that the next odd scalar degree vanishes and the next even degree is one-dimensional for each rank2–5. The proof extends the explicit commuting-pair stratification, rather than inferring this from scalar normalization. The distinct-eigenvalue open set has H1=Q and H2=0. The configuration-space proof uses a directly trivialized forgetful bundle and global logarithmic classes; averaging every two-edge wedge proves the absence of invariant H2. The two codimension-one strata have discriminant multiplicities1 and2. The resulting Borel–Moore sequence gives the stated groups.
+
+The actual complete-flag decoration kappa_(n,k) evaluates at a scalar plane and separated lines to (2k−n−1)(n−2)! w2. The proof counts its P1 components with the positive complex cross-block coefficient. Scaling transfers the actual cohomology sections to the scalar origin. The normalized morphism tau_n=kappa_(n,n)/(n−1)! defines w_n, including the previously constructed w2,w3.
+
+For binary rank(d,e), the geometric basis uses A, the outer quotient Chern class times the lowest coefficients; B, the actual lift with tau_d in the first factor when d≥2; and C, the actual lift with tau_e in the second factor when e≥2. The source dimension is1+1_(d≥2)+1_(e≥2). Complete-flag refinement gives a rank-one surjective map. The matrices are:
+
+- mu21, degree−4: (1,0).
+- mu22, degree−6: (2,−1,3).
+- mu31, degree−6: (1,1).
+- mu41, degree−8: (1,2).
+- mu23, degree−8: (3,−2,6).
+
+For the triple flags, the first two basis elements are the two suffix-determinant Chern classes X,Y times the lowest coefficients. Further basis elements are the actual internal tau lifts. The common derived flag maps give (2,2) for111, (4,3,−2) for211, and (9,6,−6,6) for221. Proper support and Chern-class naturality identifies the two parenthesizations before taking these scalar images.
+
+check_first_higher.py verifies all ten binary splits, all three displayed triple rows, the actual complete-flag component enumeration, and an explicit symmetric-group edge-swap witness for every two-edge wedge through rank5. It uses exact rational arithmetic. Those finite checks do not certify the topology or sheaf maps; their proofs are in the source closure.
+
+The native consumer includes all four scalar modules in order, with the corrected bibliography. It builds in three passes to17 pages. Pages13–17 were inspected, including the final corrected pages13–14; the preceding source and layout remain unchanged. No overfull box, undefined reference, unknown bibliography key or manuscript-firewall defect was found.
+
+No prior failed route was removed. The nonproper projected pair-incidence map remains refuted. The separate degree−4 proper Milnor reduction and its subsequent image evaluation remain frozen. The present result uses the rank-two determinant-support proof in that closure, not an unaccepted numerical higher identity.
+
+The remaining scalar coefficient degrees, odd-coefficient contributions and equivariant derived extensions remain separate. A rank-five coproduct compatibility and a holomorphic field-theory comparison are not established. All assertions in this source stop at rank5. No staging, commit, push, central reader write or standalone reader opening occurred.
